  "notes": "Whole-career review includes Soviet and Gannan years, Shanghai price controls, Taiwan security leadership, state-led development and final reforms. Mature reforms take precedence over earlier one-party repression; security restrictions survived the lifting of martial law, which did not extend to every offshore island. Economic liberalization was partial and accompanied by reservations, so it is not treated as blanket laissez-faire. His 1981 reunification aim does not answer the specific statement about a border drawn by an outside power. Family visits do not establish open borders or diaspora citizenship. Henry Liu’s assassination and the Lieyu massacre were reviewed; no personal order to murder is imputed without evidence, and the latter article carries reliability notices. Nuclear weapons capability remained contested against official assurances; Taiwan had no deployed independent nuclear arsenal. Population legislation was personally prompted, but neither general reproductive autonomy nor every provision of the final law is attributed to him. Culture, religion, minority-language, ecology, technology, labor and remaining null statements were checked against the evidence; party doctrine, relatives’ beliefs, general government practice and ceremonial assent do not fill gaps. No inferred answers.\n\nMerged with an independent claude-sonnet-5-5 audit: 1 answers taken from it, 12 agreed, 0 conflicts settled by the integrator.\n\nclaude-sonnet-5-5 notes: Independent second pass. Read: both inaugural addresses (1978, 1984), his will, the 1987 martial-law order, Taiwan Communique on the 1986 Graham interview and the draft security law, a CRS report and a 1985 news report. Government and world themes were searched; his economic, society, ecology and technology positions were not found in these texts, and the Ten Projects, population policy and nuclear questions were left to the first audit (not copied). Answers resting on what his government did rather than on his own words are low: Kaohsiung detentions, martial law, the 1987 security law. Not opened: see Blocked (CommonWealth, UPI, Medium mirror: Cloudflare block). The Time August 1985 interview and the 25 December 1985 Chinese text were not reached; the succession answer rests on a news report.",
